{
	"name": "Legacy of War",
	"type": "feature",
	"img": "icons/environment/people/charge.webp",
	"system": {
		"description": "<p>At 8th level, your reputation as a warcaster has begun to spread and provides you with one of the following benefits of your choice:</p><p><strong>Dangerous:</strong> Your eager use of destructive magic has provided you a reputation as a dangerous person. You gain expertise on intimidation and persuasion checks against people who witness you using magic of any sort but take a 1d4 penalty on deception checks against guards.</p><p><strong>Mastermind:</strong> You’re well known for cunning ploys and daring escapades that unfurl according to plan. Your prestige rating increases by 1, and you gain advantage on checks to gain an audience with someone within 2 prestige ratings of your own.</p><p><strong>Unwavering Duty:</strong> Many soldiers, sailors, and guards recognize the stern resolve in your eye and your deeds. Such characters treat you more favorably than they might otherwise, and the DC of your persuasion or deception checks against them is reduced by 5 points.</p>",
